{#
    The rail, below 768px: a bottom tab bar — Home, Subs, Add, Analytics,
    More — and a sheet holding everything else.

    `<details>` rather than a scripted drawer on purpose. It opens and closes
    with no JavaScript at all, the browser handles the keyboard, and what is
    inside it is the same list of links the rail draws — so a phone with the
    bundle blocked still reaches every page the desktop does. The sheet leads
    with the household label and the user card, which are the rail's too.

    The summary carries the active marker when the page you are on is one of
    the ones the sheet holds, so a narrow screen says where you are without
    being opened.

    Add sits in the middle, raised. Like the top bar's it wears the secondary
    fill: on a phone the page's own action is on screen beside it, and that is
    the one that takes the accent.

    `nav`    the Navigation for this page
    `shell`  the ShellContext, or null
#}
{% set can_add = can(scope, 'subscription.create') %}
<nav class="tabbar" aria-label="{{ t('nav.primary') }}">
    <ul class="tabbar-list">
        {% for link in nav.tabs %}
            <li>
                <a class="tabbar-link{{ link.active ? ' is-active' : '' }}"
                   href="{{ link.href }}"
                   {{ link.active ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' }}>
                    {{ icon(link.icon, 'nav-icon') }}
                    <span class="tabbar-label">{{ t(link.tabLabelKey) }}</span>
                </a>
            </li>

            {% if loop.index == 2 and can_add %}
                <li>
                    <a class="tabbar-add" href="/subscriptions/new" data-opens-dialog="quick-add">
                        <span class="tabbar-add-button">{{ icon('add', 'nav-icon') }}</span>
                        <span class="tabbar-label">{{ t('nav.tab_add') }}</span>
                    </a>
                </li>
            {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}

        <li>
            <details class="tabbar-more{{ nav.drawerHoldsActive ? ' is-active' : '' }}">
                <summary class="tabbar-link">
                    {{ icon('more', 'nav-icon') }}
                    <span class="tabbar-label">{{ t('nav.more') }}</span>
                </summary>

                <div class="tabbar-drawer">
                    {% if shell and shell.household %}
                        {% include 'partials/household_label.twig' with {'household': shell.household} only %}
                    {% endif %}

                    {% include 'partials/user_card.twig' with {'account': nav.account, 'user': current_user} only %}

                    {% include 'partials/nav_links.twig' with {'links': nav.drawer} only %}

                    {% include 'partials/version.twig' %}
                </div>
            </details>
        </li>
    </ul>
</nav>
